    <ferc:AuxiliaryPeakingFacilitiesIndicatorIfFacilityOperatedOnDayOfHighestTransmissionPeakDelivery id="f-3427" contextRef="c-542">true</ferc:AuxiliaryPeakingFacilitiesIndicatorIfFacilityOperatedOnDayOfHighestTransmissionPeakDelivery>
    <ferc:AuxiliaryPeakingFacilitiesIndicatorIfFacilityOperatedOnDayOfHighestTransmissionPeakDelivery id="f-3428" contextRef="c-543">true</ferc:AuxiliaryPeakingFacilitiesIndicatorIfFacilityOperatedOnDayOfHighestTransmissionPeakDelivery>
    <ferc:IndicatorStockholdersReportSubmittedOrNotPrepared id="f-3430" contextRef="c-39">Not Prepared</ferc:IndicatorStockholdersReportSubmittedOrNotPrepared>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-3432" contextRef="c-39">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; line-height: 120%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION AND OPERATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; line-height: 120%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0.1in 0.0001pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Organization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Enable Gas Transmission, LLC (&amp;quot;EGT&amp;quot;), a Delaware limited liability company, is an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer&amp;quot;). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT has a 50% ownership interest in CrossPoint Pipeline, LLC (&amp;quot;CrossPoint&amp;quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0.1in 0.0001pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;EGT is primarily engaged in the interstate transportation and storage of natural gas in Oklahoma, Texas, Arkansas, Louisiana, Missouri and Kansas and, as such, EGT is subject to the jurisdiction of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;EGT owns approximately 5,655 miles of interstate pipelines and two underground natural gas storage facilities in Oklahoma and one underground natural gas storage facility in Louisiana. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;EGT operations have a combined capacity of 29.3 billion cubic feet (&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;Bcf&amp;quot;) with a peak withdrawal rate of 0.7 Bcf/per day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;Through interconnections with other pipelines and the Perryville Hub, EGT customers have access to the Midwest and Northeast markets, as well as most of the major natural gas consuming markets east of the Mississippi River. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;EGT evaluated subsequent events through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)"&gt;April 13, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;, the date on which these accompanying financial statements were available to be issued.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Any material subsequent events that occurred during this time have been properly recognized and/or disclosed in these financial statements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-indent: 22.5pt; line-height: 120%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-indent: 22.5pt; line-height: 120%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; line-height: 120%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE B - ESTIMATES AND SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; line-height: 120%"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; line-height: 120%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;1. Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;These financial statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;quot;GAAP&amp;quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and statement of cash flows, (2) certain assets and liabilities from the regulated ratemaking process are recorded that would not be recorded under GAAP for non-regulated entities, (3) classification of certain purchase accounting-related impacts from the acquisition of Enable Midstream Partners, LP by Energy Transfer on December 2, 2021 including purchase cost allocations that are not reflected in the financial statements presented herein and (4) the treatment of the ownership interest in CrossPoint as an equity-method investment. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;2. Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-indent: 22.5pt; line-height: 120%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and the accrual for and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements, and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Although these estimates are based on management's available knowledge of current and expected future events, a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;ctual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;3. Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT has a cash management agreement with Energy Transfer which authorizes Energy Transfer or its designated affiliate to provide cash management services to EGT. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;At the close of each business day, the agreement allows for EGT to transfer funds in excess of general operating purposes to Energy Transfer or if EGT has insufficient funds to meet its general operating purposes, Energy Transfer will transfer all funds necessary to EGT. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;4. Plant Materials and Operating Supplies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Plant materials and operating supplies are carried at the lower of weighted average cost or net realizable value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Materials transferred out of warehouses are priced at weighted average cost. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;5. Natural Gas Imbalances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Natural gas imbalances occur as a result of differences in volumes of natural gas received and delivered. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT values natural gas imbalance receivables and payables at current market price. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Natural gas imbalances are generally settled in cash or made up in-kind subject to the terms of EGT's tariff with no impact on revenues.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;6. Gas Stored - Base Gas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gas stored - base gas, Account 117.1, includes the cost of recoverable gas volumes that are necessary to maintain pressure and deliverability requirements for the storage facility, using the &lt;span style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)"&gt;fixed asset accounting model established under FERC's order No. 581&lt;/span&gt;. Under this approach, gas stored - base gas volumes are classified as fixed assets and valued at historical cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;7. System Balancing Gas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gas held for system operations is recorded in System balancing gas, Account 117.2, using the inventory accounting model established under FERC's order No.&lt;span style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)"&gt;581&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)"&gt;. U&lt;/span&gt;nder this approach, system balancing gas is valued at weighted average cost. Periodically, unbalanced transactions from exchange imbalances, load balancing, or no-notice transportation transactions may create a liability position for system balancing gas and is recorded in Miscellaneous accrued liabilities, Account 242. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; margin: 0; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;8. Fuel Tracker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT has a fuel tracker mechanism whereby it recovers gas used and lost on its system via in-kind receipts of volumes from shippers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The fuel tracker mechanism for EGT has a true-up provision that any over/under recoveries of volumes are returned to or collected from shippers through prospective semi-annual adjustments to the fuel retention rates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;A regulatory asset or regulatory liability is established for the difference between the volumes collected and the volumes actually used/lost on the system. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The over/under recovered volumes are valued in Other regulatory assets, Account 182.3, or Other regulatory liabilities, Account 254, at market prices in effect at the time the net over/under recoveries were recognized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, EGT's fuel tracker has a balance of $14.7 million and $0.7 million in Other regulatory assets, Account 182.3, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;9. Electric Power Costs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT bills its customers an electric power cost (&amp;quot;EPC&amp;quot;) charge to recover the cost of power consumed by electric compressor stations and other field locations on its system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The provisions of the EPC tracker contain a true-up provision such that any over-collected or under-collected cost are refunded to, or recovered from, customers via changes in subsequent EPC rates as established by periodic EPC tracker filings with the FERC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, EGT's electric power costs have a balance of $0.5 million in Other regulatory assets, Account 182.3 and $0.1 million in Other regulatory liabilities, Account 254, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;10. Utility Plant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Additions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Ongoing additions of utility plant are stated at original cost. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT capitalizes all construction-related direct labor and material costs, as well as indirect construction costs. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Such indirect construction costs primarily include labor and related costs of departments associated with supporting construction activities and allowance for funds used during construction. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The indirect capitalized labor and related costs are largely based upon results of periodic time studies or management reviews of time allocations, which provide an estimate of time spent supporting construction projects. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The cost of replacements and betterments that extend the useful life of utility plant is also capitalized. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The cost of repairs and replacements of minor utility plant items is charged to expense as incurred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Retirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;When ordinary retirements of utility plant occur, the original cost plus cost of removal less salvage value is removed by a charge to accumulated depreciation and amortization, with no gain or loss recorded. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;When entire regulated operating units of utility plant are sold, the original cost and related accumulated depreciation and amortization accounts are removed, with any resulting gain or loss recorded in the statement of income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Depreciation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT computed depreciation expense under the composite method using FERC-approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;For general and intangible plant, EGT computed depreciation expense under the straight-line method using FERC-approved depreciation rates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Amortization related to Gas plant acquisition adjustments, Account 114, is computed using the straight-line method over the average remaining life of the related asset and included in Miscellaneous amortization, Account 425. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Allowance for Funds Used During Construction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT capitalizes the cost of funds used during construction for capital projects. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The rates used by EGT are calculated pursuant to the FERC rules, which include an allowance for the cost of debt and equity funds.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;11. Asset Retirement Obligation (&amp;quot;ARO&amp;quot;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Legal obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived assets are recorded at fair value at the time the obligations are incurred, if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Present value techniques are used which reflect assumptions such as removal and remediation costs, inflation, and profit margins that third parties would demand to settle the amount of the future obligation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT did not include a market risk premium for unforeseeable circumstances in its fair value estimates because such a premium could not be reasonably estimated. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Upon initial recognition of the liability, costs are capitalized as a part of the long-lived asset and depreciated over the useful life of the related asset. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The liability is accreted to its present value each period with accretion being recorded to operating expense or regulatory asset, as applicable, with a corresponding increase in the carrying amount of the liability. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT was not able to reasonably measure the fair value of the AROs as of December 31, 2025 or 2024 as the expected settlement dates were indeterminable. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT will record an ARO in the periods in which EGT can reasonably determine the settlement dates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: justify; background-color: unset"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;12. Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-align: justify; line-height: 120%"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Related party transactions primarily include revenues earned from and payments for services provided by Energy Transfer and its subsidiaries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Transactions are generally allocated based on relevant criteria, including time spent, utility plant, gross margin, salaries, or other appropriate methods.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;13. Environmental Expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental expenditures that relate to an existing condition caused by past operations that do not contribute to current or future revenue generation are expensed. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental expenditures relating to current or future revenues are expensed or capitalized as appropriate. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Liabilities are recorded when environmental assessments and/or clean-ups are probable and the costs can be reasonably estimated. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Remediation obligations are not discounted because the timing of future cash flow streams is not predictable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, there were no amounts accrued for future environmental expenditures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;14. Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT's revenues from transportation and storage of natural gas are based on capacity reservation charges and, to a lesser extent, commodity usage charges.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Reservation revenues, recognized monthly, are based on contracted rates and capacity reserved by the customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Revenues from commodity usage charges, also recognized monthly, are based on the volumes received from or delivered to the customer, based on EGT's tariff. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Revenues from natural gas and natural gas liquids are recognized based on volumes sold when control transfers to third parties or affiliates at market prices. Revenues collected during the pendency of a rate proceeding may be required by the FERC to be refunded in the final order.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT establishes reserves for such potential refunds, as appropriate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;No such reserves were required as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;15. Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Expected Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT has a concentration of customers in the energy segment that may impact EGT's overall exposure to credit risk, either positively or negatively, in that the customers may be similarly affected by changes in economic or other conditions. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT manages credit risk to mitigate credit losses and exposure to uncollectible trade receivables. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Prospective and existing customers are reviewed regularly for creditworthiness based upon pre-established standards consistent with FERC filed tariffs to manage credit risk within approved tolerances. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Customers that do not meet minimum credit standards are required to provide additional credit support in the form of a letter of credit, prepayment, or other forms of security. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT establishes an allowance for expected credit losses on trade receivables based on the expected ultimate recovery of these receivables and considers many factors including historical customer collection experience, general and specific economic trends and known specific issues related to individual customers, sectors, and transactions that might impact collectability. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Changes in the allowance are recorded as a component of operating expenses; reductions in the allowance are recorded when receivables are subsequently collected or written-off. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Past-due receivable balances are written-off when EGT's efforts have been unsuccessful in collecting the amount due. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EGT's allowance for expected credit losses was not material as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table presents the relative contribution to EGT's total transportation and storage revenues from operations of each customer that comprised at least 10% of its revenues:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" width="603" style="width: 452.05pt" class="e-rte-paste-table"&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;td width="64" valign="bottom" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="237" valign="bottom" style="width: 178pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="64" valign="bottom" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="88" valign="bottom" style="width: 65.85pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="64" valign="bottom" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="86" valign="bottom" style="width: 64.2pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;  &lt;/tr&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="237" style="width: 178pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="237" colspan="3" style="width: 178.05pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-left: none; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Years Ended December 31,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;  &lt;/tr&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="237" style="width: 178pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="88" style="width: 65.85pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-left: none; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="86" style="width: 64.2pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-left: none; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;  &lt;/tr&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="237" style="width: 178pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="88" style="width: 65.85pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="86" style="width: 64.2pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;  &lt;/tr&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="237" style="width: 178pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Customer   A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="88" style="width: 65.85pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;20%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="86" style="width: 64.2pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;20%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;  &lt;/tr&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="237" style="width: 178pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;Customer   B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="64" style="width: 48pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="88" style="width: 65.85pt; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; te